 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 298,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "A medicine in pregnancy or breastfeeding: is it worth it?",
   "lines": [
    "most drugs reach the baby, and most are still safe · always weigh the risk of the UNTREATED disease",
    "the risk depends on the drug, the dose, the timing, genetic susceptibility and her disease",
    "> 90% of pregnant women take a medicine (2.9 on average) · < 10% of drugs (1980–2010) have fetal risk data · < 50% of pregnancies planned",
    "counsel by context: BEFORE (planning) · DURING (taking it) · AFTER (a baby with a malformation) · unsure → FRAME clinic"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_preg",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 192,
   "w": 488,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "PREGNANT: the placenta is NOT a barrier",
   "lines": [
    "preimplantation: ALL OR NONE (miscarriage) · embryonic (organogenesis): MAJOR malformations · fetal: FUNCTIONAL defects"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_bf",
   "x": 573,
   "y": 192,
   "w": 738,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "BREASTFEEDING: how much reaches the baby, and can the baby clear it?",
   "lines": [
    "most drugs cross into milk, in minute amounts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "safe_head_0_0",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 350,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 114,
   "kind": "safe_h",
   "title": "Most drugs: probably safe",
   "lines": [
    "baseline major malformation risk 2–4%: 97% have a healthy baby",
    "causes: genetic 25% · drugs 1% · unknown 50%"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "terat_head_0_0",
   "x": 295,
   "y": 350,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 114,
   "kind": "terat_h",
   "title": "Major teratogen",
   "lines": [
    "even these harm only a fraction of exposed babies"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rid_head_0_0",
   "x": 573,
   "y": 350,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 114,
   "kind": "rid_h",
   "title": "Usually SAFE",
   "lines": [
    "most medications are not contraindicated"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ci_head_0_0",
   "x": 823,
   "y": 350,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 114,
   "kind": "ci_h",
   "title": "Contraindicated",
   "lines": [
    "a short list"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "soc_head_0_0",
   "x": 1073,
   "y": 350,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 114,
   "kind": "soc_h",
   "title": "Alcohol, tobacco, cannabis, coffee",
   "lines": [
    "not contraindicated, except as below"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "safe_clue_0_0",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 504,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 412,
   "kind": "safe_t",
   "title": "Untreated disease harms too",
   "lines": [
    "• asthma, epilepsy",
    "• depression, psychosis",
    "• infections"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "terat_clue_0_0",
   "x": 295,
   "y": 504,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 132,
   "kind": "bad",
   "title": "Biggest risk",
   "lines": [
    "• isotretinoin > 30%, thalidomide ~30%",
    "• valproate > 15% + cognitive problems",
    "• mycophenolate ~6%"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "terat_clue_1_0",
   "x": 295,
   "y": 658,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 258,
   "kind": "terat_w",
   "title": "Also",
   "lines": [
    "• carbamazepine: neural tube defect 1%",
    "• lithium: Ebstein's anomaly (1 in 5000)",
    "• warfarin: fetal warfarin syndrome (rare)",
    "• ACE inhibitors, ARBs · methotrexate · DES",
    "• alcohol · phenytoin, topiramate · methimazole · tetracycline, trimethoprim · misoprostol · lead, mercury"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rid_clue_0_0",
   "x": 573,
   "y": 504,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 412,
   "kind": "rid_t",
   "title": "Gets INTO milk if",
   "lines": [
    "• high maternal blood level, fat-soluble or transported (BCRP)",
    "• not protein-bound",
    "• small: > 500 daltons stays out (insulin > 6000, heparin 40,000; ethanol 200 gets in)",
    "• then must be absorbed from the baby's gut"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ci_clue_0_0",
   "x": 823,
   "y": 504,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 412,
   "kind": "bad",
   "title": "Avoid",
   "lines": [
    "• atenolol (renally cleared beta-blocker)",
    "• cancer drugs, radioactive iodine",
    "• cocaine, heroin"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "soc_clue_0_0",
   "x": 1073,
   "y": 504,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 412,
   "kind": "soc_t",
   "title": "Alcohol does NOT increase milk",
   "lines": [
    "keep it minimal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "safe_inv_0_0",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 956,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 272,
   "kind": "safe_w",
   "title": "A malformation is > 99 in 100 times NOT a drug",
   "lines": [
    "• put her risk in perspective: fear harms too",
    "• post-Chernobyl: 10,000–15,000 unwarranted terminations",
    "• animal data mislead: > 1200 drugs malformative in animals, not humans"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "terat_inv_0_0",
   "x": 295,
   "y": 956,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 272,
   "kind": "terat_w",
   "title": "Uncertain or overstated",
   "lines": [
    "• selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors (SSRIs): ~1%, uncertain",
    "• statins: probably a myth"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rid_inv_0_0",
   "x": 573,
   "y": 956,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 170,
   "kind": "rid_t",
   "title": "1 · Relative infant dose (RID) < 10% = safe",
   "lines": [
    "• milk concentration × 150 mL/kg/day ÷ maternal dose per kg per day",
    "• fluoxetine 1.2%",
    "• milk/plasma ratio > 1 = concentrates in milk, but often harmless"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rid_inv_1_0",
   "x": 573,
   "y": 1148,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 80,
   "kind": "rid_w",
   "title": "2 · Can the baby absorb and clear it?",
   "lines": [
    "slow clearance → it accumulates"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ci_inv_0_0",
   "x": 823,
   "y": 956,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 134,
   "kind": "ci_t",
   "title": "Why atenolol: RID ~20%",
   "lines": [
    "• newborn kidneys clear it slowly in week 1: slow heart, cyanosis",
    "• same for water-soluble acebutolol, nadolol, sotalol"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ci_inv_1_0",
   "x": 823,
   "y": 1112,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 116,
   "kind": "ci_w",
   "title": "Problematic, not forbidden",
   "lines": [
    "• lithium, amiodarone, phenobarbital",
    "• ethosuximide, ergotamine, bromocriptine"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "soc_inv_0_0",
   "x": 1073,
   "y": 956,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 134,
   "kind": "soc_w",
   "title": "Alcohol limit",
   "lines": [
    "• ≤ 0.5 g/kg (< 2 beers or 1 glass of wine)",
    "• wait ≥ 2 h before feeding",
    "• half-life lengthens at higher doses"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "soc_inv_1_0",
   "x": 1073,
   "y": 1112,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 116,
   "kind": "soc_w",
   "title": "Tobacco",
   "lines": [
    "risk is infection and sudden infant death, not the milk: not near the baby, change clothes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "safe_tx_0_0",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 1268,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 80,
   "kind": "ok",
   "title": "Treat: do NOT deny an effective drug",
   "lines": [
    "fewest drugs, as little as needed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "safe_tx_1_0",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 1370,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "warn",
   "title": "Careful with NEWER drugs",
   "lines": [
    "fetal harm often found years after release"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "terat_tx_0_0",
   "x": 295,
   "y": 1268,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 70,
   "kind": "ok",
   "title": "1 · Planning: switch FIRST",
   "lines": [
    "e.g. mycophenolate → azathioprine"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "terat_tx_1_0",
   "x": 295,
   "y": 1360,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 88,
   "kind": "warn",
   "title": "2 · Already exposed",
   "lines": [
    "counsel on timing and dose: see the ANTENATAL CARE chart"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rid_tx_0_0",
   "x": 573,
   "y": 1268,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 180,
   "kind": "ok",
   "title": "Keep the drug AND breastfeeding",
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "id": "ci_tx_0_0",
   "x": 823,
   "y": 1268,
   "w": 238,
   "h": 180,
   "kind": "bad",
   "title": "Not while breastfeeding",
   "lines": []
